<title>UK: ASDA dips as NatWest cuts to &quot;reduce&quot;.</title>
<headline>ASDA dips as NatWest cuts to &quot;reduce&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in ASDA Group Plc dipped in early trade on Thursday as analysts at NatWest Securities cut the stock to &quot;reduce&quot; from &quot;hold,&quot; market sources said.</p>
<p>ASDA shares were down 1-3/4p at 115p by 0920 GMT in volume of 1.1 million shares.</p>
<p>Sources said there was talk of pressure on margins though analysts at the brokerage could not immediately be reached for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
